Regplate.dbf
Created by Kevin Kealy 31/8/94
Please distribute freely.
This file is suitable for 3/3a.

On vehicle registration plates, the last two letters of the three letter 
group e.g. E 123 RTX or RTX 123 X
                  ^^     ^^
signify the town in which the vehicle was registered.  Irish plates are
similar, with the letters being at the front in 1,2 or 3 letter groups.
Of limited use, this can be helpful if you're a bit of an anorak - OR, if
you're buying a car in Dartford, why was it registered in County Down...?
Perhaps it's stolen...?
Anyhow, the file's easy to use.  Just type in the 2-letter code.  On the 3a,
it's helpful to "lock" the Code: field for the search, (eg WS for Bristol
will also get all the ShreWSbury entries).

Enjoy.

kkealy@cix.compulink.co.uk - 31/8/94.
